Key questions and rationale for parents.

New animals
What to do:
Create an animal cross, then present your idea to the other person.
You could draw a picture or make notes to help you with your presentation.
Things you should include in your presentation:
The two parent animals;
Which features of the new animal are inherited from which parent;
How the new animal is better adapted than its parents to a particular situation, environment or purpose;
Any ways in which the new animal might find it harder to survive than its parents;
Why you chose to make this new animal.
Which animals should I cross?

